      "id": 1,
      "text": "On the original plat, Couch left streets unnamed, marking them only with the letters of the alphabet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.livingplaces.com/OR/Multnomah_County/Portland_City/Alphabet_Historic_District.html",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Alphabet Historic District grew from six platted additions that were added to Portland in the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.livingplaces.com/OR/Multnomah_County/Portland_City/Alphabet_Historic_District.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Couch’s naval background led him to believe the area’s commercial future lay north of Oregon City, near the Willamette‑Columbia confluence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.livingplaces.com/OR/Multnomah_County/Portland_City/Alphabet_Historic_District.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Many of Couch’s clan members settled the land he claimed, creating a neighborhood for Portland’s pioneering elite.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.livingplaces.com/OR/Multnomah_County/Portland_City/Alphabet_Historic_District.html",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The district was once called the Northwest Industrial Triangle, a hub for manufacturing and distribution in early 20th‑century Portland.",
